.SH NAME
md_frontend_2node__modules_2date-fns_2docs_2release \- Releasing date-fns 
.PP


.PP
.IP "1." 4
First, make sure that the library is built by running \fR\&./scripts/build/build\&.sh\fP and committing and pushing any change you would have\&.
.IP "2." 4
Then add the changelog entry generated by \fRnpx tsx scripts/release/buildChangelog\&.ts\fP to (CHANGELOG\&.md)[\&.\&./CHANGELOG\&.md]\&. Make sure that the output is valid Markdown and fix if there're any errors\&. Commit and push the file\&.
.IP "3." 4
Using the version that the changelog script generated, run the command:

.PP
.PP
.nf
env VERSION="vX\&.XX\&.X" APP_ENV="production" GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS="secrets/production/key\&.json" \&./scripts/release/release\&.sh
.fi
.PP

.PP
The script will change \fRpackage\&.json\fP\&. \fBDo not commit the change, and reset it instead\fP\&.
.IP "4." 4
Now when the package is published, go to \fRGitHub Releases\fP and draft a new version using the changelog entry you generated earlier\&.
.IP "5." 4
Finally, write an announce tweet using the created GitHub release as the tweet link\&.
.PP

.PP
You're done, great job! 
